WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.380
Good morning Hank; it's Tuesday, March 17th
2021. It's Question Tuesday, the day that

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.450
I answer real questions from real Nerdfighters.
Let's get right to it.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:09.640
Can you start the video by telling Hank the
wrong day?

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:10.640
Sure.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.610
Is it cougish if a seventeen year old girl
goes out with a fifteen year old guy?

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:18.340
When did cougish happen? How is cougish a
thing when French the Llama continues inexplicably

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:22.150
not to be a thing? Anyway, that does not strike
me as cougish, it strikes me as completely

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:23.150
normal.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:25.400
Can you speak Dutch?
No. I keep trying to get through a whole interaction

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:30.240
with someone only speaking Dutch, so I'll
be like: "Een bier dankuwel" And the person

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.190
will be like: "I'm sorry, I don't understand
what you're saying. Do you want a beer?"

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:35.820
What's the most archaic thing you know how
to do?

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.960
Pretty good at turning magazine pages.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.690
Why didn't you show the "Good morning Hank
it's Wednesday" from Plainfield, Indiana?

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:44.610
There's something wrong with my phone, and
I can't get videos from my phone into my computer.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:48.629
Like: Insert Plainfield video... Yeah, that
didn't work.

00:00:48.629 --> 00:00:51.850
Why are pirates pirates?
Because they failed out of ninja university.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:55.830
Who the eff is Hank?
Hank is a Trans-Neptunian object 27 percent

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:59.539
more massive than Pluto. Hank was originally
named Zena, after the warrior princess, but

00:00:59.539 --> 00:01:02.650
then the scientific team that discovered Hank
decided that Hank should be named something

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.219
more astronomy-ish. Like Hank.

00:01:05.219 --> 00:01:07.999
Why haven't you done Peanut Butter Face in
a long time?

00:01:07.999 --> 00:01:09.399
I disagree with your premise.

00:01:09.399 --> 00:01:19.079
This guy is really affecting my vision. Oh
yeah, that's much better. Oh, Peanut Butter

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.079
Face.

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:21.310
What were some of the original titles of your
books?

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:24.130
Oh I'm glad I did Peanut Butter Face before
I answered the literary question. They were

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:28.869
always really pretentious, like "More Light
Than Heat" or "An Imperial Affliction". Both

00:01:28.869 --> 00:01:31.450
of which, it occurs to me, would be really
good with the 'in your pants' rule.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:34.490
Can you explain the 'in your pants' thing?
Yeah, our friend Maureen Johnson discovered

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:37.799
that book titles are funnier when you add
'in your pants' to the end of them. Like The

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:43.359
Nature of Monsters in your pants, or The Pleasures
and Sorrows of Work in your pants, or La Festa

00:01:43.359 --> 00:01:45.029
è Finita in your pants.

00:01:45.029 --> 00:01:47.389
If Henry had been a girl, what would you have
named her?

00:01:47.389 --> 00:01:50.939
The Yeti and I agreed in advance that if the
baby was a boy, he would be named Henry, and

00:01:50.939 --> 00:01:54.909
if the baby was a girl, she would be named
Bubbles the Nerdfighting Lady Baby.

00:01:54.909 --> 00:01:57.130
Are we ever gonna find out the lie from the
April Fools video?

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:58.929
Yeah, the lie was that there was no lie.

00:01:58.929 --> 00:02:01.479
How's Amsterdam?
It's great! The peanut butter is delicious!

00:02:01.479 --> 00:02:04.789
Has Helen Hunt heard the Helen Hunt song yet?
No, but did you know that Helen Hunt has a

00:02:04.789 --> 00:02:05.789
Twitter?

00:02:05.789 --> 00:02:08.200
What happens inside a black hole?
We don't really know, but scientists believe

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:12.660
that being inside of a black hole is a great
way to feel special because you're guaranteed

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:21.849
to become a singularity. Anyone? No... Singularity
jokes? It's physics. It's funny 'cause it's

00:02:21.849 --> 00:02:22.849
theoretical.

00:02:22.849 --> 00:02:27.040
Can you restock the DFTBA shirts, please?
Bing, bing, bing, bing, done. All these shirts

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.920
are back in stock at dftba.com, your independently
owned, uncorporate, deliciously disorganized,

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.290
friendly neighborhood e-tailer.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:36.849
What are the marks on your arm?
They're birth marks. Get used to them because

00:02:36.849 --> 00:02:40.340
they're gonna be around for the rest of my
life. Unless my arm gets cut off...

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.879
How do you feel about Hank being a meme?
It's not like it's a competition or anything,

00:02:43.879 --> 00:02:46.019
but just to be clear: I am also a meme.

00:02:46.019 --> 00:02:49.579
Where is Willy? Is he there with you in Amsterdam?
No. Willy's staying with the Yeti's aunt and

00:02:49.579 --> 00:02:53.760
uncle who he likes far better than he likes
me. Willy has regarded me with suspicion ever

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:58.200
since I revealed to you his inability to achieve
a full tail-rection. He may not like me very

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.319
much, but I bet he wishes he was here right
now.

00:03:00.319 --> 00:03:04.069
What is Willy's middle name?
Um...I guess technically it's Wilson Bubbles

00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:05.519
the Nerdfighting Puppy Roberts.

00:03:05.519 --> 00:03:08.890
What are we doing for Hanko de Mayo?
There is a link in the dooblydoo on this very

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:12.440
topic. Please click on it right now unless
you are Hank. Hank, if you click on that link,

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:15.640
I will cut off your fingers! Probably not;
that's an exaggeration, but there will be

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:19.640
serious consequences. There won't be any consequences,
but don't click on the link!

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.189
Shouldn't you be writing your new book right
now?

00:03:21.189 --> 00:03:23.339
Yes. Yes, I should. Hank, I'll see you on
Monday.

